---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [
    'gavin-hamilton',
    'juan-luna',
    'guillermo-tolentino',
    'elmer-borlongan',
    'juanito-torres',
  ].map((slug) => ({ params: { slug } }));
}

const artistsData = {
  'gavin-hamilton': {
    name: 'Gavin Hamilton',
    nationality: 'Scottish',
    discipline: 'Painter',
    lifespan: '1723 – 1798',
    born: 'Lanark, Scotland',
    died: 'Rome, Italy',
    image: '/artists/gavin-hamilton.jpg',
    pullQuote: '"Hamilton did not paint antiquity — he used it as a mirror for the present."',
    bio: [
      "Gavin Hamilton was born in Lanark, Scotland in 1723 and trained in Glasgow before making his way to Rome, where he would spend the greater part of his adult life. In Rome, he became a central figure in the intellectual and artistic circles that were reinventing European painting from the ground up — drawing on ancient Greece and Rome not as nostalgia but as moral instruction.",
      "Hamilton's Homeric series — of which Achilles Lamenting the Death of Patroclus is the most celebrated — established him as one of the founding architects of Neoclassicism. His canvases are monumental in scale, theatrical in composition, and deeply serious in tone. Where Rococo painters offered pleasure, Hamilton offered tragedy, heroism, and grief.",
      "He trained a generation of artists who passed through Rome and studied under him, including future titans of the movement. Jacques-Louis David absorbed Hamilton's clarity of moral purpose and his insistence that painting be about something — that it carry the weight of human consequence. In this sense, Hamilton's influence on Western art history extends far beyond what his name recognition might suggest.",
    ],
    context: "Hamilton's presence in this exhibition about Filipino cultural identity is not incidental. His Achilles entered Philippine classrooms through the colonial curriculum — a Greek story filtered through a Scottish painter, taught to Filipino students as universal literature. In absorbing this work, Filipino artistic consciousness did something remarkable: it took a foreign tradition and made it speak to its own conditions of suffering, resistance, and the cost of war.",
    works: [
      { slug: 'achilles-patroclus', title: 'Achilles Lamenting the Death of Patroclus', year: '1763', image: '/artworks/achilles-patroclus.jpg' },
    ],
    prev: null,
    next: { slug: 'juan-luna', name: 'Juan Luna', image: '/artists/juan-luna.jpg' },
  },
  'juan-luna': {
    name: 'Juan Luna',
    nationality: 'Filipino',
    discipline: 'Painter',
    lifespan: '1857 – 1899',
    born: 'Badoc, Ilocos Norte, Philippines',
    died: 'Hong Kong',
    image: '/artists/juan-luna.jpg',
    pullQuote: '"Luna did not ask permission to be great. He demanded it — and Europe conceded."',
    bio: [
      "Juan Luna y Novicio was born in 1857 in Badoc, Ilocos Norte, and from the beginning demonstrated a technical facility that set him apart from his contemporaries. He studied at the Academia de Dibujo y Pintura in Manila before making his way to Europe, first to Madrid and then to Rome, where he immersed himself in the grand tradition of European academic painting.",
      "His masterwork, the Spoliarium, was exhibited at the Exposicion Nacional de Bellas Artes in Madrid in 1884. It won the gold medal — the first ever awarded to a Filipino artist at such a prestigious European competition.",
      "Jose Rizal, who was present in Madrid during this period, recognized immediately what Luna had done. In his famous banquet toast, Rizal called the Spoliarium a poem of condemnation and grief — an indictment of colonial rule rendered in the language of Rome.",
    ],
    context: "Luna's significance for Filipino identity cannot be overstated. In a colonial context where Filipino culture was systematically devalued, Luna's triumph at Madrid was political as much as artistic. He mastered European technique and turned it against the power structure that had colonized his homeland.",
    works: [
      { slug: 'spoliarium', title: 'Spoliarium', year: '1884', image: '/artworks/spoliarium.jpg' },
    ],
    prev: { slug: 'gavin-hamilton', name: 'Gavin Hamilton', image: '/artists/gavin-hamilton.jpg' },
    next: { slug: 'guillermo-tolentino', name: 'Guillermo Tolentino', image: '/artists/guillermo-tolentino.jpeg' },
  },
  'guillermo-tolentino': {
    name: 'Guillermo Tolentino',
    nationality: 'Filipino',
    discipline: 'Sculptor',
    lifespan: '1890 – 1976',
    born: 'Malabon, Manila, Philippines',
    died: 'Quezon City, Philippines',
    image: '/artists/guillermo-tolentino.jpeg',
    pullQuote: '"To sculpt in marble is to speak in the language of permanence. Tolentino chose that language to say Filipino things."',
    bio: [
      "Guillermo Estrella Tolentino was born in Malabon in 1890 and would go on to become the most consequential sculptor in Philippine history. He trained at the Philippine School of Arts and Trades before winning a government scholarship to study in Rome.",
      "In Rome, Tolentino developed not just technical mastery but a philosophy. He understood that the European sculptural tradition was a language — and that he could speak it with a Filipino accent.",
      "His two works in this exhibition represent opposite ends of his creative range: the Diwata and the Jose Rizal Bust, which effectively defined the visual face of Filipino nationalism for generations.",
    ],
    context: "Tolentino was declared National Artist of the Philippines for Sculpture in 1973 — a recognition of the way his work shaped how Filipinos see themselves. His sculptures occupy the plazas, schools, and public buildings of the Philippines as arguments: about who Filipinos are, what they value, and what they refuse to forget.",
    works: [
      { slug: 'diwata', title: 'Diwata', year: '1931', image: '/artworks/diwata.jpg' },
      { slug: 'rizal-bust', title: 'Jose Rizal Bust', year: '1911', image: '/artworks/rizal-bust.jpg' },
    ],
    prev: { slug: 'juan-luna', name: 'Juan Luna', image: '/artists/juan-luna.jpg' },
    next: { slug: 'elmer-borlongan', name: 'Elmer Borlongan', image: '/artists/elmer-borlongan.jpg' },
  },
  'elmer-borlongan': {
    name: 'Elmer Borlongan',
    nationality: 'Filipino',
    discipline: 'Painter',
    lifespan: 'b. 1967',
    born: 'Manila, Philippines',
    died: null,
    image: '/artists/elmer-borlongan.jpg',
    pullQuote: '"Borlongan paints the Philippines that exists — not the one politicians promise."',
    bio: [
      "Elmer Borlongan was born in Manila in 1967 and studied at the University of the Philippines College of Fine Arts, where he developed the expressionist approach that would define his mature work.",
      "His figures are working people: market vendors, laborers, migrants, the urban poor. He renders them with a combination of monumental physicality and raw tenderness — his brushwork is urgent, almost violent, but his subjects are depicted with profound dignity.",
      "The Battle of Mactan represents a departure from his usual urban settings. In applying his contemporary expressionism to a 16th-century subject, Borlongan insists that the past is not over.",
    ],
    context: "Borlongan occupies a unique position in this exhibition as the only living artist represented. His work bridges the historical and the contemporary — connecting the colonial and revolutionary past to the present conditions of Filipino life.",
    works: [
      { slug: 'battle-of-mactan', title: 'Battle of Mactan', year: '2004', image: '/artworks/battle-of-mactan.jpg' },
    ],
    prev: { slug: 'guillermo-tolentino', name: 'Guillermo Tolentino', image: '/artists/guillermo-tolentino.jpeg' },
    next: { slug: 'juanito-torres', name: 'Juanito Torres', image: '/artists/juanito-torres.jpg' },
  },
  'juanito-torres': {
    name: 'Juanito Torres',
    nationality: 'Filipino',
    discipline: 'Painter',
    lifespan: 'b. 1969',
    born: 'Philippines',
    died: null,
    image: '/artists/juanito-torres.jpg',
    pullQuote: '"Torres paints the people history forgot — and refuses to let you look away."',
    bio: [
      "Juanito Torres is a Filipino painter associated with the KAMPILAN movement — a collective of artists committed to the principle that art must serve the people, not the market.",
      "His approach to portraiture is distinctive: his subjects are never isolated from their social context. Heroism, in Torres's visual language, is collective.",
      "His General Malvar portrait gives us Malvar embedded in the people he led — the general and the masses rendered with equal care, equal weight, equal dignity.",
    ],
    context: "Torres's inclusion in this exhibition serves an important function: he draws attention to the gaps in official historical memory. General Malvar is not a figure who appears in most Western accounts of Philippine history. Torres's painting is an act of recovery.",
    works: [
      { slug: 'general-malvar', title: 'General Malvar: Lider ng Masang Pilipino', year: '2002', image: '/artworks/general-malvar.jpg' },
    ],
    prev: { slug: 'elmer-borlongan', name: 'Elmer Borlongan', image: '/artists/elmer-borlongan.jpg' },
    next: null,
  },
};

const { slug } = Astro.params;
const artist = artistsData[slug as keyof typeof artistsData];
---

<Layout title={`${artist.name} | Culture & Identity`}>
  <main class="artist-page">

    <section class="artist-hero">
      <div class="hero-image-col">
        <div class="hero-img-wrap">
          <img src={artist.image} alt={artist.name} class="hero-img" />
          <div class="img-overlay"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="lifespan-badge"><span>{artist.lifespan}</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-text-col">
        <div class="hero-text-inner">
          <p class="hero-eyebrow">The Artist</p>
          <h1 class="hero-name">{artist.name}</h1>
          <div class="hero-divider"></div>
          <div class="hero-tags">
            <span class="hero-tag">{artist.nationality}</span>
            <span class="tag-sep">·</span>
            <span class="hero-tag">{artist.discipline}</span>
          </div>
          <dl class="hero-vitals">
            <div class="vital-item">
              <dt>Born</dt>
              <dd>{artist.born}</dd>
            </div>
            {artist.died && (
              <div class="vital-item">
                <dt>Died</dt>
                <dd>{artist.died}</dd>
              </div>
            )}
          </dl>
          <a href="/artists" class="back-link">← All Artists</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="pull-quote-wrap reveal">
      <blockquote class="pull-quote">
        <p>{artist.pullQuote}</p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <article class="bio-section">
      <div class="bio-label-col">
        <p class="section-label">Biography</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bio-text-col">
        {artist.bio.map((para) => (
          <p class="bio-para reveal">{para}</p>
        ))}
      </div>
    </article>

    <section class="context-block reveal">
      <div class="context-inner">
        <p class="context-label">Significance for this Exhibition</p>
        <p class="context-text">{artist.context}</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="works-section">
      <div class="works-header reveal">
        <h2 class="works-heading">Works in This Exhibition</h2>
      </div>

      {artist.works.length === 1 && (
        <a href={`/artworks/${artist.works[0].slug}`} class="work-card-single reveal">
          <div class="work-img-wrap">
            <img src={artist.works[0].image} alt={artist.works[0].title} class="work-img" />
            <div class="work-gradient"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="work-info">
            <p class="work-year">{artist.works[0].year}</p>
            <h3 class="work-title">{artist.works[0].title}</h3>
            <span class="work-cta">View work →</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      )}

      {artist.works.length > 1 && (
        <div class="works-grid">
          {artist.works.map((work, i) => (
            <a href={`/artworks/${work.slug}`} class={`work-card reveal reveal-delay-${i + 1}`}>
              <div class="work-img-wrap">
                <img src={work.image} alt={work.title} class="work-img" />
                <div class="work-gradient"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="work-info">
                <p class="work-year">{work.year}</p>
                <h3 class="work-title">{work.title}</h3>
                <span class="work-cta">View work →</span>
              </div>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      )}
    </section>

    <nav class="artist-nav">
      {artist.prev ? (
        <a href={`/artists/${artist.prev.slug}`} class="artist-nav-item">
          <div class="nav-thumb-wrap">
            <img src={artist.prev.image} alt={artist.prev.name} class="nav-thumb" />
          </div>
          <div class="nav-info">
            <span class="nav-direction">← Previous Artist</span>
            <span class="nav-name">{artist.prev.name}</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      ) : <div />}

      {artist.next ? (
        <a href={`/artists/${artist.next.slug}`} class="artist-nav-item nav-next">
          <div class="nav-info nav-info-right">
            <span class="nav-direction">Next Artist →</span>
            <span class="nav-name">{artist.next.name}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="nav-thumb-wrap">
            <img src={artist.next.image} alt={artist.next.name} class="nav-thumb" />
          </div>
        </a>
      ) : <div />}
    </nav>

  </main>
</Layout>

<script>
  const revealEls = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add('visible');
          observer.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.1 }
  );
  revealEls.forEach((el) => observer.observe(el));
</script>

<style>
  .artist-page { padding-top: 80px; }

  .artist-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    min-height: 90vh;
  }
  .hero-image-col { position: relative; overflow: hidden; background: #1c1917; }
  .hero-img-wrap { position: absolute; inset: 0; }
  .hero-img {
    width: 100%; height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover; object-position: center top;
    transition: transform 6s ease;
  }
  .artist-hero:hover .hero-img { transform: scale(1.04); }
  .img-overlay {
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(to right, rgba(28,25,23,0.15) 0%, rgba(28,25,23,0.0) 100%);
  }
  .lifespan-badge {
    position: absolute; bottom: 2.5rem; left: 2.5rem;
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 300;
    color: #f2ead8; letter-spacing: 0.15em;
  }

  /* Dark right panel — all text is light, no readability issues */
  .hero-text-col {
    background: #1c1917;
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    padding: 5rem 5rem 5rem 6rem;
  }
  .hero-text-inner { max-width: 440px; width: 100%; }

  .hero-eyebrow {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.45em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: #f2ead8; opacity: 0.5;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem; display: block;
  }
  .hero-name {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 4vw, 4.5rem);
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.0; color: #f2ead8;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .hero-divider {
    width: 32px; height: 2px; background: #8b1a1a; margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }
  .hero-tags { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .hero-tag {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #f2ead8; opacity: 0.6;
  }
  .tag-sep { color: #f2ead8; opacity: 0.25; }

  .hero-vitals { list-style: none; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .vital-item { margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
  .vital-item dt {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.58rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #f2ead8; opacity: 0.4;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .vital-item dd {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: #f2ead8; opacity: 0.85; font-weight: 300; margin: 0;
  }
  .back-link {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none; color: #8b1a1a;
    display: inline-block; transition: opacity 0.2s ease; opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .back-link:hover { opacity: 1; }

  .pull-quote-wrap { max-width: 820px; margin: 5rem auto; padding: 0 4rem; }
  .pull-quote {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.2vw, 1.65rem);
    font-weight: 400; font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6; color: #1c1917;
    border-left: 3px solid #8b1a1a; padding: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem 2.5rem; margin: 0;
  }

  .bio-section {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; gap: 5rem;
    max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 4rem 6rem;
  }
  .bio-label-col { padding-top: 0.3rem; }
  .section-label {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.4em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #1c1917; opacity: 0.45;
    position: sticky; top: 120px;
  }
  .bio-para {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.95; font-weight: 300; color: #1c1917; opacity: 0.82;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem; max-width: 680px;
  }

  .context-block { background: #1c1917; padding: 5rem 4rem; }
  .context-inner { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .context-label {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.38em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #f2ead8; opacity: 0.45; margin-bottom: 1.75rem; display: block;
  }
  .context-text {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.9; color: #f2ead8; opacity: 0.85; font-weight: 300;
  }

  .works-section { padding: 6rem 4rem; max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .works-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem; padding-bottom: 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.1);
  }
  .works-heading {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 400;
    margin: 0; color: #1c1917;
  }

  .work-card-single {
    position: relative; overflow: hidden; display: block;
    text-decoration: none; color: #f2ead8; background: #1c1917;
    width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16/7;
  }
  .work-card-single .work-img-wrap { position: absolute; inset: 0; }
  .work-card-single .work-img {
    width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover;
    transition: transform 0.8s ease, filter 0.4s ease; filter: brightness(0.72);
  }
  .work-card-single:hover .work-img { transform: scale(1.03); filter: brightness(0.58); }
  .work-card-single .work-gradient {
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(28,25,23,0.92) 0%, rgba(28,25,23,0.2) 50%, transparent 100%);
  }
  .work-card-single .work-info { position: absolute; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; padding: 3rem 3rem 2.5rem; }
  .work-card-single .work-cta { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.3s ease; }
  .work-card-single:hover .work-cta { opacity: 1; }

  .works-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(320px, 1fr)); gap: 2px; }
  .work-card {
    position: relative; overflow: hidden; display: block;
    text-decoration: none; color: #f2ead8; background: #1c1917; aspect-ratio: 4/3;
  }
  .work-img-wrap { position: absolute; inset: 0; }
  .work-img {
    width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover;
    transition: transform 0.8s ease, filter 0.4s ease; filter: brightness(0.75);
  }
  .work-card:hover .work-img { transform: scale(1.05); filter: brightness(0.6); }
  .work-gradient {
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(28,25,23,0.9) 0%, transparent 55%);
  }
  .work-info { position: absolute; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; padding: 2rem 2rem 1.75rem; }
  .work-year {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.3em; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: 0.55; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .work-title {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .work-cta {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #8b1a1a;
    opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.3s ease; display: block;
  }
  .work-card:hover .work-cta { opacity: 1; }

  .artist-nav { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; border-top: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.1); }
  .artist-nav-item {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem; padding: 2.5rem 4rem;
    text-decoration: none; color: #1c1917; transition: background 0.3s ease;
  }
  .artist-nav-item:hover { background: rgba(28,25,23,0.04); }
  .nav-next { border-left: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.1); justify-content: flex-end; }
  .nav-thumb-wrap {
    width: 64px; height: 64px; overflow: hidden;
    flex-shrink: 0; background: #ddd4c0; border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .nav-thumb {
    width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center top; transition: transform 0.4s ease;
  }
  .artist-nav-item:hover .nav-thumb { transform: scale(1.08); }
  .nav-info { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; }
  .nav-info-right { text-align: right; }
  .nav-direction {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #1c1917; opacity: 0.45;
  }
  .nav-name { font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 500; color: #1c1917; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .artist-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; min-height: unset; }
    .hero-image-col { min-height: 60vw; }
    .hero-text-col { padding: 3rem 2rem; }
    .hero-name { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 8vw, 3rem); }
    .bio-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; padding: 0 2rem 4rem; }
    .bio-label-col { display: none; }
    .pull-quote-wrap { padding: 0 2rem; margin: 3.5rem auto; }
    .context-block { padding: 3.5rem 2rem; }
    .works-section { padding: 4rem 2rem; }
    .work-card-single { aspect-ratio: 4/3; }
    .artist-nav { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .nav-next { border-left: none; border-top: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.1); justify-content: flex-start; }
    .artist-nav-item { padding: 2rem; }
  }
  .artist-page {

  background-color: #f2ead8; /* ADD THIS */
}
</style>